        "date": "2026-11-21T01:00:49Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): judge a rotary kind's first rapid on the spindle C from the turret's index position\n\nA Rotary Contour, Parallel or Offset whose path states the spindle C\nposts only through a post that declares liveTooling (the lathe post):\nG00 C with the turret at its index position, then G00 X Z to the first\npoint. The new seam operation/rotary_traverse.rs reads that rapid with\n#3077's live-tool law right after the C stamp, on a mill-turn or a\nlathe. The work and a chuck are read at C's angle; fixed steel is read\nin the machine frame, on the +X station (the c_steel convention). A hit\nis refused by name. An unstamped rotary kind on a mill-turn posts\nthrough the mill post and now takes the mill laws. The caches take the\nop-stamp word live-traverse-rotary-3096.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/3096-mill-turn-rotary-first-traverse.md\n\nFixes #3096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
